<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, oil down, meal strong.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, oil down, meal strong.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets in very limited trading activity on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soybean arrivals were poor due to the close of the financial year as purchasers had run out of funds. Soybean markets will be closed for Good Friday and will open on Monday.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was down by 100 rupees per tonne on selling pressure from plants. Demand from hydrogenated vegetable oil manufacturing units was limited. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were strong in local market on better demand but prices were steady in export. Soymeal yellow was $304-305 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $115-116 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,000 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
